\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. I could not do without Thee,
\par O Saviour of the lost,
\par Whose precious blood redeemed me
\par At such tremendous cost;
\par Thy righteousness, Thy pardon,
\par Thy precious blood must be
\par My only hope and comfort,
\par My glory and my plea.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I could not do without Thee,
\par I cannot stand alone,
\par I have no strength or goodness,
\par No wisdom of my own;
\par But Thou, beloved Saviour,
\par Art all in all to me,
\par And weakness will be power
\par If leaning hard on Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I could not do without Thee;
\par No other friend can read
\par The sp[irit's strange deep longings,
\par interpreting its need;
\par No human heart could enter
\par Each dim recess of mine,
\par And soothe, and hash, and calm it,
\par O blessed Lord, but Thine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. I could not do without Thee;
\par For years are fleeting fast,
\par And soon in solemn loneness
\par The river must be passed:
\par But Thou wilt never leave me;
\par And though the waves roll high,
\par I know Thou wilt be near me 
\par And whisper: It is I. \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

